# Copy to .env and fill in. Nothing here belongs in a committed file, and no
# credential value ever appears in a scenario, a target definition or a tool
# argument — targets.yaml records only variable *names*.

# Workspace root holding scenarios/, policy/, results/
AGENTSEC_WORKSPACE=.

# Recorded on every audit row. CI should set this to something like ci:<actor>.
AGENTSEC_ACTOR=local

# Optional: relocate the SQLite results file
# AGENTSEC_DB=/var/lib/agentsec/agentsec.db

# Set to 1 on any internet-reachable gateway. Refuses every non-read-only tool
# at the dispatcher, so start_run is absent rather than merely discouraged.
# AGENTSEC_MCP_READ_ONLY=1

# Comma-separated hosts exempt from the private-address check. Leave unset
# unless you genuinely need a public endpoint, and record why in review.
# AGENTSEC_ALLOW_EXTERNAL_HOSTS=

# --- Per-target credentials, referenced by name from policy/targets.yaml ---
# WAZUH_INDEXER_USER=admin
# WAZUH_INDEXER_PASSWORD=
# ORDER_AGENT_TENANT_A_TOKEN=
# ORDER_AGENT_TENANT_B_TOKEN=
